text: |-
  Conclusions
  1. A neck muscle-only trajectory for a .30-06 would have been
  through-and-through. EXTREMELY HIGH CONFIDENCE
  2. There's virtually no chance that a neck bone involved trajectory
  would have stopped a .30-06. HIGH CONFIDENCE
  3. The gel-block shots recreate Kirk's shirt movements and necklace
  breaking almost perfectly. HIGH CONFIDENCE that a supersonic,
  high energy rifle round killed Charlie Kirk
  4. The audio data we have from 9/10/25 is fully supportive of a
  supersonic round, almost certainly fired from a rifle. HIGH
  CONFIDENCE
  5. Hypothesis: to get a .30-06 round to stop in Charlie's body, as has
  been claimed, would require a very steep shot into his neck area.
  - Or, possibly, an exotic .30-06 round.
  6. If Tyler Robinson's defense does not adopt this data, they are in on
  the fix
  0:02 / 0:13 )
